Have you seen [the combine middleware helper](https://hono.dev/docs/middleware/builtin/combine)? I think it would work with `some`

Alternatively, you could create a helper hook and use both approaches, 

```typescript
import { some } from 'hono/combine'

const whenContentType = (contentType: "json" | "form") => (result, c) => {
   // Pretend i used the correct contenttype strings
   if (c.req.contentType !== contentType) { 
      // validation doesn't matter
      return undefined;
   }
}.

new App()
 .post(
    some(
      zValidator('json', whenContentType("json")),
      zValidator('form', whenContentType("form")),
    ),
   async (c) => {
      const valid = c.req.valid("json") ?? c.req.valid("form")
   }
 )
```
